This reads `*p` after `++p`. If `p` was at `unit.end - 1`, then `++p` makes `p == unit.end`, and the check `p == unit.end` should catch it. But wait, the check is `p == unit.end || ...` - if `p == unit.end` is true, the `||` short-circuits and `*p` is not evaluated. So that's fine.

